rstly obtained by preparing three complexes with different concentration gradients using water saturated octanol solution. Subsequently, 1 mg of the complexes added to a mixture of 1 mL water and1 mL octanol. Then the mixture was shaken in a thermostatic shaker (150 rpm/min and 300 K) for 24 h. Centrifugation at 1000 rpm for 5 min was allowed to stand pending separation of the upper and lower layers. UV-Vis spectra was used to determine the concentration of the complex in the organic phase (Co), the concentration of the complex in the H2O phase Cw = Ctotal–Co, finally the logP = log(Co/Cw) value was obtained."}]}